---
title: Scallion pancakes
servings: 4
yield: 3 pancakes
tags: [chinese, vegetarian, lunar new year]
cuisine: chinese
time: 1 hour
source: Cong You Bing Scallion Pancakes with Dipping Sauce by Sarah, The Woks of Life, https://thewoksoflife.com/scallion-pancakes/
---

== Pancakes ==

Stir the @all-purpose flour{1 1/2%cup} and @water{1/2%cup}(hot) together in a
#mixing bowl{} until a dough forms.

Knead it on a floured counter ~{5%minutes}, until smooth. Put it back in the
bowl, cover, and rest ~{30%minutes}. Make the sauce meanwhile.

Cut the dough into three. Roll each into a 7-inch round, giving it a quarter
turn after each pass.

Brush a round with @vegetable oil{}, then scatter over @salt{} and the
@scallions{2}(thinly sliced). Roll it up into a log, coil the log into a
snail, and flatten it to a 6-inch pancake. Press a third of the
@toasted sesame seeds{1%tbsp} into the top. Repeat with the other two.

> Keep them thick; rolled too thin they lose their layers.

Heat about a tablespoon of oil in a #nonstick pan{} or #cast-iron skillet{}.
Fry each pancake ~{3%minutes} a side, until golden brown. Cut into wedges.

== Dipping sauce ==

Mix the @soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @black vinegar{1%tsp}(Chinese), @water{1%tbsp},
@granulated sugar{1/8%tsp}, @garlic{1%clove}(finely minced) and
@scallions{1%tbsp}(chopped). Serve with the pancakes.
